Given the function $f(x) = x - 4\sqrt{x} + 4$ ($x \geq 4$), its inverse function is denoted as $f^{-1}(x)$. The sequence $\{a_n\}$ satisfies: $a_1 = 1$, $a_{n+1} = f^{-1}(a_n)$, ($n \in \mathbb{N}^*$), and the sequence $b_1, b_2 - b_1, b_3 - b_2, \ldots, b_n - b_{n-1}$ is a geometric sequence with the first term being 1 and the common ratio being $\frac{1}{3}$.  
(I) Prove that the sequence $\{\sqrt{a_n}\}$ is an arithmetic sequence;  
(II) If $c_n = \sqrt{a_n} \cdot b_n$, find the sum of the first $n$ terms of the sequence $\{c_n\}$, denoted as $S_n$.

