\\(① \frac {1}{1×2}= \frac {1}{2}\\);

\\(② \frac {1}{1×2}+ \frac {1}{2×3}= \frac {2}{3}\\);

\\(③ \frac {1}{1×2}+ \frac {1}{2×3}+ \frac {1}{3×4}= \frac {3}{4}\\);

... ,

Please write out the nth equation \_\_\_\_\_\_.

Given the following conditions: $\left(1\right)y=f\left(x\right)$ intersects with $y=2x$; $\left(2\right)$ the derivative of the function $f\left(x\right)$ is ${f'}\left(x\right)$, and the values of ${f'}\left(x\right)$ are all within the interval $\left(0,2\right)$. We denote the set of functions that simultaneously satisfy the above two conditions in the domain as $U$. Which of the following statements are correct?  
① If $f\left(x\right)\in U$, then the equation $f\left(x\right)=2x$ has exactly one solution;  
② For the function $g\left(x\right)=2\ln x$, $\left(x \gt 1\right)$, $g\left(x\right)\in U$, but $g\left(x\right)+3\notin U$;  
③ Let $h\left(x\right)\in U$, for any $x_{1}$ and $x_{2}$ in the domain of $h\left(x\right)$ such that $|x_{1}-2023| \lt 1$ and $|x_{2}-2023| \lt 1$, then $|h(x_{1})-h(x_{2})| \lt 4$.

Given that $α$ is an angle in the second quadrant, $f(α)= \frac{\sin (π-α)\tan (-α-π)}{\sin (π+α)\cos (2π-α)\tan (-α)}$.
(I) Simplify $f(α)$;
(II) If $\cos (α- \frac{3π}{2})=-\frac{1}{3}$, find the value of $f(α)$.

Given that the eccentricity of the ellipse $y=x+1$ is equal to $\frac{MD}{\sin \angle DTM}=\frac{TD}{\sin \angle TMD}$, and the focus of the parabola $\frac{MC}{\sin \angle ATM}=\frac{TC}{\sin \angle TMC}$ is the vertex of the ellipse.

(I) Find the equations of the ellipse $\pi - \angle TMD$ and the parabola $\frac{MD}{MC}=\frac{TD}{TC}$;

(II) A line $l$ passes through the point $\frac{TD}{TC}=\frac{BD}{AC}$ and intersects the parabola $\frac{MD}{MC}=\frac{TD}{TC}$ at points $P$ and $Q$. The tangents to the parabola $\frac{MD}{MC}=\frac{TD}{TC}$ at points $P$ and $Q$ are drawn. When $x^2+y^2=\rho^2, x=\rho \cos \theta, y=\rho \sin \theta$, find the equation of line $l$.

Given two fixed points A(-2, 0) and B(1, 0), let point P be a moving point such that \(|PA| = 2|PB|\). If the curve C is the locus of point P and line l passes through the point (0, -3) intersecting curve C at two distinct points D(\(x_1\), \(y_1\)) and E(\(x_2\), \(y_2\)).

(Ⅰ) Find the equation of the locus of curve C;
(Ⅱ) Determine the range of the slope of the line l;
(Ⅲ) If \(x_1x_2 + y_1y_2 = 3\), find \(|DE|\).

Given that point P is outside the plane of the parallelogram ABCD, if $$\overrightarrow {AB}$$\=(2，-1，-4), $$\overrightarrow {AD}$$\=(4，2，0), $$\overrightarrow {AP}$$\=(-1，2，-1). Determine the correct statement(s) among the following:
① AP ⊥ AB;
② AP ⊥ AD;
③ $$\overrightarrow {AP}$$ is the normal vector of plane ABCD;
④ $$\overrightarrow {AP}$$ ∥ $$\overrightarrow {BD}$$.

