In the rectangular coordinate system, establish a polar coordinate system with the coordinate origin as the pole and the positive semi-axis of the $x$-axis as the polar axis. The equation of the curve $C_{1}$ is given by $ρ=2\cos θ+2\sin θ$, and the parameter equation of the line $C_{2}$ is given by $\begin{cases} x=-1+t \\ y=-1-t \end{cases} (t \text{ is the parameter})$.
