Given a circle $O: x^{2}+y^{2}=3m^{2} (m > 0)$, and a parabola $C: y^{2}=2mx (m > 0)$. Let $P$ be the intersection point of circle $O$ and parabola $C$ in the fourth quadrant, and $N$ be the intersection point of circle $O$ with the negative half of the $y$-axis. The point $R$ is symmetric to point $N$ with respect to point $P$. Extend line $OR$ to intersect the parabola at point $Q$.

