(2) If for any $x_{1}, x_{2} \in \mathbb{R}$, the inequality $f(x_{1}) \geq g(x_{2})$ always holds, find the range of the real number $a$.

Given that the function $f(x)$ is defined on the domain $[-1,1]$, and for any $x, y \in [-1,1]$, we have $f(x+y)=f(x)+f(y)$, and when $x > 0$, we have $f(x) > 0$.
(1) Prove that the function $f(x)$ is an odd function;
(2) Discuss the monotonicity of the function $f(x)$ on the interval $[-1,1]$.

Given that the set $M$ consists of all functions $f(x)$ that satisfy the following property: there exist real numbers $a$ and $k(k \neq 0)$, such that for any $x$ in the domain, $f(a+x)=kf(a-x)$ holds. The pair $(a,k)$ is called the "accompanying pair" of the function $f(x)$.

$(1)$ Determine whether $f(x)=x^{2}$ belongs to set $M$, and explain the reason;

$(2)$ If the function $f(x)=\sin x \in M$, find all the "accompanying pairs" of the function $f(x)$ that satisfy the condition;

Given that $F\_1$ and $F\_2$ are the left and right foci of the ellipse $E$: $\frac{x^2}{a^2} + \frac{y^2}{b^2} = 1$ $(a > b > 0)$, and the line $l$ with a slope of $1$ passing through $F\_1$ intersects $E$ at points $A$ and $B$. The distances $|AF\_2|$, $|AB|$, and $|BF\_2|$ form an arithmetic sequence.
(1) Find the eccentricity of $E$;
(2) Let point $P(0, -1)$ satisfy $|PA| = |PB|$, find the equation of $E$.

